// ── A: a boot-time device upload whose whole image can exceed the
// source-custody budget copies through a reusable bounded host stage;
// the device destination is one allocation and its addresses never
// change. ──
fn slice_b322_boot_stage_upload() -> Vec<KernelRule> {
    vec![KernelRule {
        rule_id: "checkpoint-boot-staged-upload-bounded-bytes".to_string(),
        gpu_concept: "MECHANISM (the boot-upload host-stage bound; category A — MemoryAccess, the transfer/staging family): a boot-time device upload whose whole image can exceed the source-custody budget copies through a REUSABLE bounded host stage instead of reserving the entire image — the device destination stays ONE allocation at the full image size, peak host custody stays at the chunk bound, and the scale/pointer map entries are computed from the same accumulating offset, so device addresses are UNCHANGED from the whole-image form. Source: ashhart/TensorFold @ 7fce15ce #1643 (Apache-2.0). THE BOUND, verbatim [in-diff] host_stage.zig: `pub const upload_chunk: usize = 64 << 20;` — 64 MiB, an in-diff constant. THE UPLOAD LOOP, verbatim [in-diff] cuda_weights.zig: `offset = 0;` `for (items) |n| { var from: usize = 0; while (from < n.bytes.len) { const len = @min(n.bytes.len - from, @import(\"host_stage.zig\").upload_chunk); const copy = try w.source.take(d, len); @memcpy(copy, n.bytes[from..][0..len]); w.dirty = true; try w.source.copyTo(buf, offset + from, .{ .d = d, .handle = null }); from += len; } offset += n.bytes.len; }` — the device buffer is ONE allocation (`cuda.DeviceBuffer.alloc(d, total)`), and the scale/pointer map entries are computed from the same accumulating `offset`, so addresses are UNCHANGED from the whole-image form. THE STAGE IS REUSED — `source.take(d, len)` per chunk; the stage grows only when a request exceeds the kept size. THE NUANCE (author \"reuses\", never \"adds\"): the wait-before-reuse is PRE-EXISTING inside `Stage.take` (copy_source.zig: `pub fn take(...) { try s.wait(); ...`). THE FAILURE CONTRACTS are retained when a later chunk fails, verbatim test arms [in-diff] load_chunk_test.zig: `try t.expectError(error.NotReady, weights.upload(&driver, &b));` / `try t.expectError(error.NotReady, weights.close());` / poison: `try t.expect(weights.get(b.out.items[0].name) == null);` / custody: `try t.expect(mock.pinned != null); try t.expectEqual(@as(usize, 0), mock.freed);` — upload errors, close errors, the failed item stays poisoned, and the opened source stays pinned with NOTHING freed. FAKE-DRIVER TEST COVERAGE [in-diff]: exact bytes per copy (fills 0x12/0x87, per-copy content validated), destination offsets (`dst == 256 + copied`), paired ownership (`left.ptr + first == right.ptr`, one buffer: `weights.bufs.items.len == 1`), digest preserved (SHA-256 of item 0 == left.sha256). THE PERSISTENT-FORMS UPLOAD rides the same stage (forward.zig chunk loop, the same @min pattern, `f.uploads.copyTo(...)`). WHY: whole-image reservation breaks the CUDA source-custody budget at real pack sizes (multi-GB); the chunked form keeps peak host custody at 64 MiB while the device destination is byte-identical. Distinct from drain-device-work-before-free (gpu_111 — device-work lifetime before freeing; THIS is the upload-path HOST stage bound), from immutable-operand-device-resident-per-buffer-type (gpu_144, A — the placement quadrant, init-once device residency; THIS is the transfer CHUNKING), and from host-pointer-buffer-foreign-range-subtraction (gpu_90, B231 — pinning semantics of host-wrapped buffers; THIS is bounded chunk transfer). REGIME: boot/weight-load H2D copies over multi-GB packs. ANTI-REGIME: single small copies (chunking overhead dominates); DMA engines with their own bounds. NotBenchable here (host-custody/peak-memory axis — the fixture pins chunk partitioning, byte-exactness across chunk boundaries, offset accumulation, and the failed-chunk custody contracts). Source: ashhart/TensorFold @ 7fce15ce #1643 — host_stage.zig, cuda_weights.zig, load_chunk_test.zig, copy_source.zig, forward.zig, Apache-2.0. Batch 322 / Plan 322. RIDER (Batch 323 / Plan 323 — the PINNED-MAPPED STAGING face, ashhart/TensorFold GLM loader @ ab366b1e+a72b9d00+af2909ce, Apache-2.0): the stage half of this law carried into a PINNED MAPPED host buffer — 192 MiB (`pub const staging_bytes: usize = 192 << 20;`, `cuda.HostBuffer.allocMapped`) written piece-to-piece by 8 packer threads (`default_packers = 8`, TF_GLM_LOAD_PACK override max 16; piece size = a multiple of the packers when that many fit, else >= 1), the GPU copying each piece up while the packers fill the next (one stream wait per piece — the fake-driver test asserts 3 waits for 5 experts in pieces of 2+2+1, bytes identical to the one-thread pack). The whole-image pageable form it replaces, verbatim [in-commit] a72b9d00: 'copied into the loader's host bytes and then uploaded from pageable memory through the copy source's staging' (2.04 GB/rank at TP=2); 16 read-ahead readers keep ahead of the packers (MEASURED: 99 s -> 61 s at the pinned-staging step alone, then 61 s -> 51 s at TP=2, same tokens). The READER-DEPTH half (read-ahead pipeline depth keyed to the consumers' stall) is io/rust_perf-shaped -> YIELDS to plan-310 (live to 2026-10-31T14:21Z), recorded as intel. Count-neutral face, Batch 323 / Plan 323.".to_string(),
        ref_shape: "// naive: the boot reserves the WHOLE image on the host first, then\n// copies it in one call — peak host custody == the whole pack\n// (multi-GB), and a pack bigger than the source-custody budget can\n// never boot at all\nfn upload_whole_image(items: &[Item]) -> Result<DeviceWeights, Upload> {\n    let mut host = Vec::new();            // the WHOLE image reserved up front\n    for n in items {\n        host.extend_from_slice(&n.bytes); // multi-GB peak custody\n    }\n    let buf = DeviceBuffer::alloc(host.len())?; // device: one alloc (fine)\n    buf.copy_from_host(0, &host)?;        // the HOST side breaks the budget\n    Ok(DeviceWeights { buf })\n}".to_string(),
        opt_pattern: "// optimized: ONE device allocation at the full size, a REUSABLE\n// bounded host stage, and the accumulating offset builds the\n// scale/pointer map — device addresses unchanged from the whole-image\n// form\nconst UPLOAD_CHUNK: usize = 64 << 20; // [in-diff] host_stage.zig\n\nfn upload_chunked(\n    items: &[Item],\n    stage: &mut Stage,\n    map: &mut Vec<(&str, usize)>,\n) -> Result<DeviceWeights, Upload> {\n    let total: usize = items.iter().map(|n| n.bytes.len).sum();\n    let buf = DeviceBuffer::alloc(total)?; // device: ONE alloc, full size\n    let mut offset = 0usize;\n    for n in items {\n        let mut from = 0usize;\n        while from < n.bytes.len {\n            let len = (n.bytes.len - from).min(UPLOAD_CHUNK);\n            let copy = stage.take(len);          // REUSED; grows only on demand\n            copy.copy_from_slice(&n.bytes[from..][..len]);\n            buf.copy_to(offset + from, copy)?;   // dst == offset + from\n            from += len;\n        }\n        map.push((n.name, offset)); // the same accumulating offset\n        offset += n.bytes.len;      // item bases accumulate\n    }\n    Ok(DeviceWeights { buf })\n}".to_string(),
    }]
}

// ── B: a boot with cache + session identities threads the digest the
// cache was keyed with to the second consumer — one hash per byte per
// boot; the uncached path still reads once. ──
fn slice_b322_boot_identity_read_once() -> Vec<KernelRule> {
    vec![KernelRule {
        rule_id: "boot-identity-hash-read-once".to_string(),
        gpu_concept: "MECHANISM (the boot identity-digest thread; category B — Compute, the digest-reuse family): a boot with prepared-cache + session-disk both set hashed every pack byte TWICE — once for the cache key, once again for the session store's checkpoint identity (the second pass reading from disk after the weights evicted the page cache). The fix THREADS the digest the open cache was KEYED with to the other identity consumer: one hash per byte per boot; the uncached path still reads once. Source: ashhart/TensorFold @ 618625fd (Apache-2.0). THE DEFECT SITE, verbatim [in-diff] cuda_model.zig: `m.sessions = try sg.Sessions.init(gpa, io, &m.f, &bp, so, .{ .slots = m.slots, .ds_blocks = ds_blocks, .checkpoint = if (so.disk != null) try prepared.packDigest(io, &m.pack) else null });` — repaired to `... .checkpoint = if (so.disk != null) try prepared.packIdentity(io, &m.pack, if (cache) |*c| c else null) else null });`. THE THREADING, verbatim [in-diff] prepared.zig: `/// The pack's content identity the key holds, for the other owners that need it (``packDigest`` reads every byte)` + the field `pack_digest: [32]u8,` + `/// The pack's content digest: an open cache's, else read here (``packDigest`` reads every byte).` + `pub fn packIdentity(io: Io, p: *const pack_mod.Pack, cache: ?*const Cache) ![32]u8 { if (cache) |c| return c.pack_digest; return packDigest(io, p); }`. WHY THE CACHE HAS IT: `Cache.open(gpa, io, dir, pack_digest, key, write, verify)` mixes the digest into the cache key (`h.update(&pack_digest)` inside open); `Cache.fromEnv` obtains it via `open(gpa, io, dir, try packDigest(io, p), key, ...)` — one read. THE HERMETIC TEST, verbatim: `\"Pack identity: a boot with the prepared cache reads the pack's bytes once, not again for sessions\"` — `pack.dir = \"/nonexistent-dsv41-pack\"` (any real read ⇒ FileNotFound); with a cache keyed `@splat(7)`, `packIdentity` returns `@splat(7)`; with `null`, `try std.testing.expectError(error.FileNotFound, packIdentity(io, &pack, null));`. HONESTY CAVEAT (carry it): the \"190 GiB pack / minutes per rank / page-cache eviction\" narrative is COMMIT-MESSAGE-level only — the diff carries the mechanism; this entry authors the mechanism and cites the narrative as message-level provenance. Distinct from verify-once-at-trust-boundary (gpu_03, D — removes duplicate VERIFICATION EVENTS at a trust boundary, returns a capability type; THIS threads an identity DIGEST between consumers of the same computed value — compose, never merge: that rule's own kinship note names commit-over-maintained-item-digests as the digest-reuse composer and THIS is the boot-time instance of that axis), and from commit-over-maintained-item-digests (gpu_03, B — digest-of-digests makes each commit hash CHEAP; THIS eliminates a second FULL-PAYLOAD read at boot). REGIME: any boot/load path where two components independently hash the same immutable bytes (cache key + integrity identity + provenance pin). ANTI-REGIME: consumers needing a DIFFERENT hash function; mutable content (the cache key would not stay valid). NotBenchable here (page-cache/IO axis; the fixture pins the read-once behavior hermetically — a poisoned store that errors on second read + digest equality). Source: ashhart/TensorFold @ 618625fd — cuda_model.zig, prepared.zig, the pack-identity hermetic test, Apache-2.0. Batch 322 / Plan 322.".to_string(),
        ref_shape: "// naive: the boot computes the pack identity TWICE — the cache open\n// hashes every byte for its key, then the session store hashes every\n// byte AGAIN for its checkpoint identity (from disk: the weights just\n// evicted the page cache)\nfn boot_naive(pack: &Pack, io: &Io) -> Result<Boot, BootErr> {\n    let cache = Cache::from_env(io, pack)?;          // read 1: packDigest\n    let sessions = Sessions::init(io, pack,\n        Some(pack_digest(io, pack)?));               // read 2: same bytes\n    Ok(Boot { cache, sessions })\n}".to_string(),
        opt_pattern: "// optimized: the digest the cache was KEYED with is threaded to the\n// other identity consumer — one hash per byte per boot; the uncached\n// path still reads exactly once\nfn pack_identity(io: &Io, pack: &Pack, cache: Option<&Cache>) -> Result<Digest, BootErr> {\n    if let Some(c) = cache {\n        return Ok(c.pack_digest);   // the open cache already holds it\n    }\n    pack_digest(io, pack)           // no cache: read here, once\n}\n\nfn boot_prepared(pack: &Pack, io: &Io) -> Result<Boot, BootErr> {\n    let cache = Cache::from_env(io, pack)?;            // the ONE read, at open\n    let sessions = Sessions::init(io, pack,\n        Some(pack_identity(io, pack, Some(&cache))?)); // threaded, no read\n    Ok(Boot { cache, sessions })\n}".to_string(),
    }]
}

// ── D: on a vendor compiler with a known miscompile, pass shared-memory-
// staged operands BY VALUE into the vendor intrinsic and apply the
// vendor's scheduling attribute — work around the compiler bug at the
// call shape, never by dropping the intrinsic. ──
fn slice_b322_vendor_workaround() -> Vec<KernelRule> {
    vec![KernelRule {
        rule_id: "vendor-intrinsic-staged-operands-by-value-scheduling-attribute".to_string(),
        gpu_concept: "MECHANISM (the vendor-compiler workaround at the call shape; category D — Dispatch): on a vendor compiler with a known miscompile, pass shared-memory-staged operands BY VALUE into the vendor intrinsic and apply the vendor's scheduling attribute — work around the compiler bug at the call shape, never by dropping the intrinsic. Source: ggml-org/llama.cpp @ 792fcf4e #31341 \"opencl: add initial iq1 support\" (MIT, author shaoqi@qti.qualcomm.com — Qualcomm). THE HAZARD COMMENT, VERBATIM (appears TWICE — iq1_s AND iq1_m dp4a kernels): `// Pass staged operands by value; local dp4a operands miscompile on X2.` THE SCHEDULING ATTRIBUTE, VERBATIM: `__attribute__((qcom_wave_pair_mode(1)))` on `kernel void kernel_gemm_noshuffle_iq1_s_q8_1_dp4a(` and the iq1_m twin. THE MECHANISM AS OBSERVED: activations staged in `__local` shared memory (`__local uint4 sh_qa4[TILESIZE_N][2]` + `barrier(CLK_LOCAL_MEM_FENCE)`), then loaded into register `uint4` values and passed BY VALUE into the inline dot function (`inline int dot8_q8a_v(uint8 qw, uint4 a0, uint4 a1)`) — the Qualcomm packed dp4a intrinsic `dot_acc_sat_4x8packed_ss_int(qw.s0, a0.x, r)` under `#ifdef cl_khr_integer_dot_product`. THE PER-PATH ADMISSION LADDER around it (ggml-opencl.cpp): decode gemv (n==1) → dp4a (refuses n<=1, non-contiguous, misaligned offset1; gate `const int tile_n = n <= 8 ? 8 : 32;` — the narrow kernel via `-DTILESIZE_N=8` recompile) → noshuffle gemm. HONESTY: zero measured perf numbers in the entire diff — the per-path table is structural. WHY (inferred from the workaround shape, LABEL AS INFERENCE): the miscompile is in the vendor compiler's handling of __local-pointer operands to the dp4a intrinsic on Adreno X2; by-value register operands + wave-pair scheduling keep the intrinsic. Distinct-from (no close corpus family — the vendor-hazard workaround class lands here first; said honestly): the shape/dtype predicate-gating family (popcorn — gates fast paths on shape/dtype predicates to avoid miscompiles on edge shapes — DIFFERENT axis: that is OUR predicate gating, THIS is a VENDOR-compiler bug worked around at the call shape), and silent-narrow-index (the gpu_02 faces — silent wrong results; THIS is a vendor miscompile with a targeted workaround, not an address-width law). REGIME: kernels calling vendor-specific intrinsics (dp4a-class) on silicon with known vendor-compiler bugs; mobile/OpenCL lanes. ANTI-REGIME: portable intrinsic paths; compilers without the hazard (the attribute is vendor-specific and harmless elsewhere only if the vendor documents it so). NotBenchable here (correctness/vendor-compiler axis). Source: ggml-org/llama.cpp @ 792fcf4e #31341 — the iq1_s + iq1_m dp4a OpenCL kernels + the ggml-opencl.cpp admission ladder, MIT. Batch 322 / Plan 322.".to_string(),
        ref_shape: "// naive: the dot helper takes the staged operands as references into\n// the __local stage (the pointer shape) and the kernel carries no\n// scheduling attribute — the call shape the vendor compiler\n// miscompiles on Adreno X2; the tempting 'fix' drops the intrinsic\n// for scalar math (the loss the workaround refuses)\nfn dot8_local_ptr(stage: &LocalStage, i0: usize, i1: usize, qw: u8) -> i32 {\n    let mut r = 0i32;\n    // every operand read goes back through the __local pointer:\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, stage.qa4[i0].x, &mut r); // miscompiles on X2\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, stage.qa4[i0].y, &mut r);\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, stage.qa4[i1].x, &mut r);\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, stage.qa4[i1].y, &mut r);\n    r\n}\n// kernel_gemm_noshuffle_iq1_s_q8_1_dp4a: no scheduling attribute".to_string(),
        opt_pattern: "// optimized: the hazard comment's own law — load the staged operands\n// into registers and pass them BY VALUE, and carry the vendor\n// scheduling attribute; the intrinsic stays\n// __attribute__((qcom_wave_pair_mode(1)))   // [in-diff] verbatim\n// kernel void kernel_gemm_noshuffle_iq1_s_q8_1_dp4a(...)\nfn dot8_q8a_v(qw: u8, a0: U4, a1: U4) -> i32 { // by VALUE (registers)\n    let mut r = 0i32;\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, a0.x, &mut r); // the packed intrinsic, under\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, a0.y, &mut r); // cl_khr_integer_dot_product\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, a1.x, &mut r);\n    dot_acc_sat(qw, a1.y, &mut r);\n    r\n}\n\nfn dp4a_tile(stage: &LocalStage, i0: usize, i1: usize, qw: u8) -> i32 {\n    // the stage -> register hand-off BEFORE the vendor call:\n    let a0 = stage.qa4[i0];\n    let a1 = stage.qa4[i1];\n    dot8_q8a_v(qw, a0, a1)\n}\n\n// the admission ladder stays structural: tile_n = n <= 8 ? 8 : 32 (the\n// narrow kernel recompiles with -DTILESIZE_N=8); dp4a refuses n<=1,\n// non-contiguous, misaligned offset1".to_string(),
    }]
}

pub fn entries() -> Vec<KernelRule> {
    let mut out = Vec::new();
    out.extend(slice_b322_boot_stage_upload());
    out.extend(slice_b322_boot_identity_read_once());
    out.extend(slice_b322_vendor_workaround());
    out
}
